From: canoziia <canoziia@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] lmcache: derive the MP worker rank when one server is shared

One LMCache server can serve several engines of the same (model_name,
world_size): the layout registry is keyed by that pair, and the PD roles in
these deployments are homogeneous by construction (identical layer partition,
identical chunk geometry).

Rank resolution preferred the mp_worker_rank layout hint and otherwise used the
server-side device index, which only holds when a server sees a single engine
(indices 0..world_size-1). A server shared by two PP2 engines sees the second
engine's GPUs at indices 2 and 3, so registration aborted with a bare
ValueError. Fold the index into [0, world_size) for that case and log the
resolution (instance, model, device, hint, result) so a mis-derivation is
diagnosable from the server log.

--- a/lmcache/v1/multiprocess/modules/lmcache_driven_transfer.py
+++ b/lmcache/v1/multiprocess/modules/lmcache_driven_transfer.py
@@ -992,11 +992,33 @@
         attn_desc = kv_groups_manager.get_attn_desc()
         # Prefer the logical rank supplied by the paired vLLM client. The
         # device-index fallback only supports legacy single-node clients.
-        worker_rank = (layout_hints or {}).get(
-            "mp_worker_rank", cache_context.device.index
-        )
+        hinted_rank = (layout_hints or {}).get("mp_worker_rank")
+        worker_rank = None
+        if hinted_rank is not None:
+            try:
+                worker_rank = int(hinted_rank)
+            except (TypeError, ValueError):
+                worker_rank = None
+            if worker_rank is not None and not 0 <= worker_rank < world_size:
+                worker_rank = None
         if worker_rank is None and world_size == 1:
             worker_rank = 0
+        if worker_rank is None:
+            # Shared-server fallback: one server may serve several engines of the
+            # same (model_name, world_size). The server-side device index then runs
+            # past world_size for the later engines while ranks repeat per engine,
+            # so fold the index back into the rank range.
+            worker_rank = cache_context.device.index % world_size
+        logger.info(
+            "register_kv_cache rank resolution: instance=%s model=%s "
+            "world_size=%s device=%s hint=%r -> worker_rank=%s",
+            instance_id,
+            model_name,
+            world_size,
+            cache_context.device,
+            hinted_rank,
+            worker_rank,
+        )
         if worker_rank is None or not 0 <= worker_rank < world_size:
             raise ValueError(
                 "Cannot derive MP worker rank from registered cache device "
